# Build context exclusions for the gateway image (root Dockerfile).
#
# There was no .dockerignore until 2026-07-31. Measured on the machine that
# wrote this file, the un-ignored context was ~11.8 GB: .claude 9.9 GB,
# .git 903 MB, website 817 MB (node_modules 584 MB + .next 231 MB),
# .mypy_cache 94 MB. Every byte of that was transferred to the daemon on every
# build even though the Dockerfile COPYs only four paths.
#
# The image itself was also polluted: `COPY src ./src` shipped 406 __pycache__
# files, including .pyc compiled by CPython 3.14 into a 3.12 image.
#
# The gateway build needs exactly: pyproject.toml, src/, migrations/,
# alembic.ini. Nothing else here is required by any stage.

# --- VCS + agent/session state ----------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github
.claude
.ds-sync

# --- Python build/test/tool caches ------------------------------------------
# NOTE the `**/` prefixes. .dockerignore patterns are anchored at the context
# root, so a bare `__pycache__` would exclude only a top-level directory of
# that name and would leave every src/skylize/**/__pycache__ in place — which
# is precisely the pollution this file exists to stop.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info
.eggs
build
dist
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.hypothesis
.grimp_cache
.import_linter_cache
.coverage
htmlcov
.tox
.nox

# --- Virtualenvs -------------------------------------------------------------
.venv
venv
env

# --- Frontend: not part of the gateway image --------------------------------
website
node_modules

# --- Tests: not installed by the wheel, not run in the image ----------------
tests

# --- Infra + docs: not read from /app at runtime (verified: no reference to
#     /app/infra anywhere in src/). Keeping terraform state, compose files and
#     the docs tree out of a runtime image is also the right blast radius.
infra
docs
policy
scripts
*.md

# --- Local secrets and editor cruft. `.env` must never enter an image: the
#     process reads .env from its CWD (/app), so a leaked file would silently
#     override the injected Secrets Manager values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
.playwright-mcp

# --- Terraform state, should it ever be produced locally ---------------------
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
.terraform
